<h1>About</h1>
<p class="lead mt-3">
  Welcome to <strong>BibleBytes</strong>, a blog dedicated to exploring
  prophecies from the Bible that have been scientifically proven and validated
  over time. This platform is designed to shed light on these fascinating
  correlations, making the connection between ancient texts and modern
  discoveries.
</p>

<hr class="border-secondary my-4" />

<h3 class="mt-4">About the Developer</h3>
<p>
  My name is <strong>Vlad Ebert</strong>, and I built this blog from scratch as
  part of my journey to learn web development. This project allowed me to
  understand how to create and manage a blog platform, and to deepen my
  knowledge in backend and frontend development.
</p>

<hr class="border-secondary my-4" />

<h3 class="mt-4">Technologies and Features Used</h3>
<ul class="list-unstyled">
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Node.js & Express:</strong> For server-side logic and routing.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>EJS (Embedded JavaScript):</strong> To render HTML views
    dynamically.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Bootstrap:</strong> For responsive and modern UI design.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Body-Parser:</strong> To handle form submissions and parse data.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>File System (fs):</strong> To read and write data persistently in
    <code>posts.json</code>.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>CRUD Operations:</strong> Full Create, Read, Update, and Delete
    functionality for blog posts.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>JSON Storage:</strong> All posts are saved in a JSON file for
    persistence.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Confirm Delete with JavaScript:</strong> A safety step to avoid
    accidental deletions.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Static Files:</strong> CSS and JavaScript served from the
    <code>public</code> directory.
  </li>
</ul>

<hr class="border-secondary my-4" />

<h3 class="mt-4">Recent Additions to the Project</h3>
<ul class="list-unstyled">
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Responsive Mobile Navigation:</strong> Added a collapsible
    hamburger menu for mobile screens.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Express-EJS-Layouts:</strong> Used layout templates for a
    consistent page structure.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Dynamic Page Titles:</strong> Each page now sends a title to be
    shown in the browser tab.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Continue Reading:</strong> Articles display only a preview on the
    blog page with a link to full view.
  </li>
  <li class="mb-2">
    ✅ <strong>Edit Post:</strong> Edit button opens a form prefilled with
    current title and content.
  </li>
</ul>

<hr class="border-secondary my-4" />

<h3 class="mt-4">Future Improvements</h3>
<p>
  In the future, I plan to extend this blog with features like search
  functionality, pagination, and a proper database like MongoDB to store
  articles securely. I am also considering adding user authentication and
  comment sections.
</p>
